        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "6e08b47f-15de-5ea6-ab4d-8ec50526a0a8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Susanna Thompson, Rob Reiner, Alec Baldwin, Whoopi Goldberg, James Woods, Stephen Amell, Willa Holland, David Ramsey, Colin Donnell, Katie Cassidy, Paul Blackthorne, Diane Ladd\n- Works: Ghosts of Mississippi, Little Giants, Random Hearts, Dragonfly, Once and Again, Arrow, Pilot\n- Roles: Karen Sammler, Moira Queen, Oliver Queen, Thea Queen, John Diggle, Tommy Merlyn, Laurel Lance, Quentin Lance\n\nFacts:\n- Susanna Thompson was born on January 27, 1958, and is an American actress.\n- Susanna Thompson appeared in the film Little Giants in 1994.\n- Ghosts of Mississippi is a 1996 American biographical courtroom drama film directed by Rob Reiner and starring Alec Baldwin, Whoopi Goldberg, and James Woods.\n- Susanna Thompson and Diane Ladd both appeared in the 1996 film Ghosts of Mississippi.\n- Diane Ladd appeared in the film Primary Colors in 1998.\n- Susanna Thompson played Karen Sammler on the ABC drama series Once and Again from 1999 to 2002.\n- Susanna Thompson appeared in the film Random Hearts in 1999.\n- Diane Ladd appeared in the film 28 Days in 2000.\n- Susanna Thompson appeared in the film Dragonfly in 2002.\n- In the Arrow episode Pilot, Susanna Thompson played Moira Queen, the mother of Oliver Queen, who was played by Stephen Amell.\n- In the Arrow episode Pilot, Willa Holland played Thea Queen, David Ramsey played John Diggle, Colin Donnell played Tommy Merlyn, Katie Cassidy played Laurel Lance, and Paul Blackthorne played Detective Quentin Lance.\n- Diane Ladd appeared in the film American Cowslip in 2008.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "996dbb10-abd7-571c-b5dc-c3a927592cd0",
        "text": "Page: Susanna Thompson. Sentence: Susanna Thompson (born January 27, 1958) is an American actress.\nPage: Susanna Thompson. Sentence: She is known for her roles in films \"Little Giants\" (1994), \"Ghosts of Mississippi\" (1996), \"Random Hearts\" (1999) and \"Dragonfly\" (2002), and as Karen Sammler on ABC drama series \"Once and Again\" (1999–2002).\nPage: Ghosts of Mississippi. Sentence: Ghosts of Mississippi is a 1996 American biographical courtroom drama film directed by Rob Reiner and starring Alec Baldwin, Whoopi Goldberg, and James Woods.\nPage: Pilot (Arrow). Sentence: The episode introduces Oliver Queen (Stephen Amell), a billionaire playboy, his mother Moira Queen (Susanna Thompson), sister Thea (Willa Holland), new bodyguard John Diggle (David Ramsey), best friend Tommy Merlyn (Colin Donnell), ex-girlfriend Laurel Lance (Katie Cassidy), and her father Detective Quentin Lance (Paul Blackthorne).\nPage: Diane Ladd. Sentence: Her other film appearances include \"Chinatown\" (1974), \"Ghosts of Mississippi\" (1996), \"Primary Colors\" (1998), \"28 Days\" (2000), and \"American Cowslip\" (2008).",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
